00:34:31.059 --> 00:34:33.380
Like we're not like, we're not like showbiz fans.
就像我们不像演艺圈的粉丝一样。

00:34:33.380 --> 00:34:34.219
You know what I mean?
你知道我的意思？

00:34:34.219 --> 00:34:42.059
So when you first start meeting these people, like one of my first shows was, I played one of Sally Field's law clerks in the show called The Court.
因此，当你第一次开始见到这些人时，就像我的第一场演出一样，我在名为《法庭》的节目中扮演莎莉·菲尔德的一名法律职员。

00:34:42.059 --> 00:34:48.739
And, you know, it took me like a little while to just be able to say two sentences to her, right?
而且，你知道，我花了很长时间才能够对她说两句话，对吧？

00:34:48.739 --> 00:34:54.579
But then you work with people, you see their process, you see them work and you see, oh, they're doing what I'm doing.
但是当你与人们一起工作时，你会看到他们的流程，你会看到他们的工作，你会发现，哦，他们正在做我正在做的事情。

00:34:54.579 --> 00:34:56.900
Like they're analyzing a script, they're doing their best.
就像他们在分析剧本一样，他们正在尽力而为。

00:34:56.900 --> 00:34:59.219
They just, I've just watched them for a lot of years.
他们只是，我已经看了他们很多年了。

00:34:59.219 --> 00:35:03.780
And it's also strange, because now people watch me for a lot of years and they have all sorts of weird.
这也很奇怪，因为现在人们观察我很多年了，他们有各种各样的奇怪之处。

00:35:03.780 --> 00:35:07.579
I was gonna say, you're getting the receiving end of that.
我想说的是，你已经收到了。

00:35:07.579 --> 00:35:24.900
But I remember, it actually gives me compassion for people who the floor drops out underneath them when they see someone they know from TV or movies, because I remember that I had the same response when I started out, but it's very good, I think, to work with actors you've long admired.
但我记得，这实际上让我同情那些在看到电视或电影中认识的人时脚下的地板掉下来的人，因为我记得当我刚开始时也有同样的反应，但我认为与你长期钦佩的演员合作非常好。

00:35:24.900 --> 00:35:29.099
Most of the time, they're incredibly lovely and just really professional.
大多数时候，他们非常可爱而且非常专业。

00:35:29.099 --> 00:35:34.579
But it's nice to write size them because you feel, you don't feel as much of a golf between you and them.
但写下他们的尺寸是很好的，因为你觉得，你和他们之间的感觉不那么像打高尔夫球了。

00:35:34.579 --> 00:35:36.059
And you're like, you know what?
你就像，你知道吗？

00:35:36.059 --> 00:35:37.780
We're both professional actors.
我们都是专业演员。

00:35:37.780 --> 00:35:40.739
We're both employed on this show and we're gonna do our work together.
我们都受雇于这个节目，我们会一起做我们的工作。

00:35:40.739 --> 00:35:41.579
And it's really fun.
这真的很有趣。

00:35:41.579 --> 00:35:42.420
I don't know.
我不知道。

00:35:42.420 --> 00:35:44.340
I always considered it a thrilling part of the job.
我一直认为这是工作中令人兴奋的部分。

00:35:44.340 --> 00:35:50.940
Living in LA does that, because you sort of like, you also sort of realize like, No, this person just lives in a neighborhood in LA.
住在洛杉矶就能做到这一点，因为你有点喜欢，你也有点意识到，不，这个人只是住在洛杉矶的一个社区。

00:35:50.940 --> 00:35:53.800
They go to a Ralph's, like they, you know?
他们像他们一样去拉尔夫百货，你知道吗？

00:35:53.800 --> 00:36:05.280
My wife has this funny thing where she really wants to believe that the characters are like in middle ages or whatever, like if she's watching, you know, Game of Thrones, I mean, she's like, don't tell me they get smoothies in her one.
我妻子有一件有趣的事情，她真的很想相信这些角色就像中世纪或其他什么，就像如果她正在看，你知道，权力的游戏，我的意思是，她就像，别告诉我他们在她的里面喝了冰沙。

00:36:05.280 --> 00:36:06.280
I don't wanna know.
我不想知道。

00:36:06.280 --> 00:36:07.679
I don't wanna know that.
我不想知道这个。

00:36:07.679 --> 00:36:09.719
They ruined the illusion for me.
他们毁了我的幻想。

00:36:09.719 --> 00:36:10.719
So, yeah.
所以，是的。

00:36:10.719 --> 00:36:18.280
Who was, can you guys remember the first, is that, was that head of the class one, your first like moment like that, Josh and Carter, I want to know your first, if that way.
你们还记得第一个是谁吗，是那个班长，你们第一次像这样的时刻，乔什和卡特，我想知道你们的第一个，如果是这样的话。

00:36:18.280 --> 00:36:20.039
Do you remember your first one, Carter?
卡特，你还记得你的第一个吗？

00:36:20.039 --> 00:36:25.480
I remember, it's very similar too, because I grew up in suburban Ohio, as did Josh.
我记得，这也非常相似，因为我和乔什一样在俄亥俄州郊区长大。

00:36:25.480 --> 00:36:33.800
And I remember reading that William Cat, the greatest American hero, was going to be in a play.
我记得读到过，美国最伟大的英雄威廉猫将出演一部戏剧。

00:36:33.800 --> 00:36:35.960
He was in a play at a Cleveland Playhouse.
他在克利夫兰剧院演出。

00:36:35.960 --> 00:36:36.800
Yeah.
是的。

00:36:36.800 --> 00:36:40.199
And I read that, clocked it, and forgot about it.
我读了这篇文章，记下了它，然后就忘记了。

00:36:40.199 --> 00:36:48.360
And I lived in a town called Shaker Heights, which is like a few towns away from the, but it's like a nice town.
我住在一个叫Shaker Heights 的小镇，离这里有几个小镇远，但它就像一个不错的小镇。

00:36:48.360 --> 00:36:53.260
It's kind of, it's connected to everything with like the rapid transit, like the trail, the light rail.
它与一切事物都有联系，比如快速交通、步道、轻轨。

00:36:53.260 --> 00:36:58.889
And so I sort of clocked that that he's gonna be in it and forgot it.
所以我猜想他会参与其中，然后就忘记了。

00:36:58.889 --> 00:37:05.119
And then I'm like walking around my neighborhood, like on a suburban street on a sidewalk, no one else around.
然后我就像在我的社区周围散步，就像在郊区街道的人行道上一样，周围没有其他人。

00:37:05.119 --> 00:37:08.340
And there's a guy coming on the side, side line.
有一个人从旁边过来，边线。

00:37:08.340 --> 00:37:12.159
Was he coming the opposite direction, coming towards me, flying, flying at me.
他是不是从相反的方向过来，朝我这边来，飞来飞去，朝我飞来。

00:37:12.159 --> 00:37:13.860
No, but he walked by.
没有，但他走过了。

00:37:13.860 --> 00:37:15.059
And it was William Cat.
那是威廉猫。

00:37:15.059 --> 00:37:21.559
And it was like, that was the first like, celebrity I ever saw, like, that was a, yeah.
就像，这是我见过的第一个名人，就像，那是，是的。

00:37:21.559 --> 00:37:22.920
There's nothing else to that story either.
这个故事也没有其他的事情了。

00:37:22.920 --> 00:37:23.760
I didn't say hi.
我没有打招呼。

00:37:23.760 --> 00:37:25.760
No, but that's a fucking iconic moment.
不，但这真是一个标志性的时刻。

00:37:25.760 --> 00:37:29.239
That's like, that is totally, that's a huge moment, man.
这就像，这完全是一个重要的时刻，伙计。

00:37:29.239 --> 00:37:30.280
And Howard Hesman, actually.
事实上，还有霍华德·赫斯曼。

00:37:30.280 --> 00:37:34.559
Howard Hesman was, he was in a play at the Cleveland Playhouse also.
霍华德·赫斯曼也在克利夫兰剧院演出。

00:37:34.559 --> 00:37:43.760
And I remember like, I saw him on stage and like, I think I may have like gotten to sign like my program and like, that was like a huge deal.
我记得，我在舞台上看到他，我想我可能会像我的节目一样签名，这就像一件大事。

00:37:43.760 --> 00:37:54.500
Mine, I think mine, the New York Mets lived in my hometown, some of them in Port Washington, New York, like during the 86, 87 seasons, and I would see them around.
我的，我想我的，纽约大都会队住在我的家乡，其中一些在纽约华盛顿港，就像在86、87赛季一样，我会在周围看到他们。

00:37:54.500 --> 00:37:57.719
I know this is an actor's, but it was just like, I see them on TV, and here they are.
我知道这是一个演员的作品，但这就像，我在电视上看到他们，而他们就在这里。

00:37:57.719 --> 00:38:04.739
And one time we saw like Billy Joel driving around, I'm like, I just remember those are my first ones of like, oh, these people exist in the real world.
有一次我们看到像比利乔尔这样的人开车到处走，我就想，我只记得那些是我的第一个，哦，这些人存在于现实世界中。

00:38:04.739 --> 00:38:09.579
But then the funny thing is you think you get inured to it in LA, living in LA for years.
但有趣的是，你认为你已经习惯了洛杉矶的生活，在洛杉矶生活了很多年。

00:38:09.579 --> 00:38:12.340
And then, but every now and again, one really gets you.
然后，但时不时地，有人真正抓住了你。

00:38:12.340 --> 00:38:15.179
Like we've been living in LA for a couple of years, doing how I met your mother.
就像我们在洛杉矶生活了几年一样，就像我遇见你母亲一样。

00:38:15.179 --> 00:38:25.940
We had our own TV show, and I was walking down the street one day, and I passed the actor, James Marsden, I think, no, James Marsters, forgive me, who played Spike in Buffy.
我们有自己的电视节目，有一天我走在街上，我经过了演员詹姆斯·麦斯登，我想，不，詹姆斯·马斯特斯，请原谅我，他在《巴菲》中扮演斯派克。

00:38:25.940 --> 00:38:28.019
I'm a huge Buffy vampire slayer fan.
我是吸血鬼杀手巴菲的超级粉丝。

00:38:28.019 --> 00:38:33.940
And here I was like a professional, I think I was a show runner at the time, living in Los Angeles, and he's walking up to me, and I go, Spike!
在这里我就像一个专业人士，我想我当时是一名节目主持人，住在洛杉矶，他朝我走来，我走了，斯派克！

00:38:33.940 --> 00:38:35.900
Like the dorkiest fucking fan in the world.
就像世界上最愚蠢的粉丝一样。

00:38:35.900 --> 00:38:42.300
I call him his character name, I forgot he's clearly uncomfortable, and then I was like, that was, I guess you never fully let go of it.
我称他为他的角色名字，我忘记了他显然不舒服，然后我想，那就是，我猜你从未完全放开它。

00:38:42.300 --> 00:38:45.860
Every now and again, one's just gonna catch you and you're gonna be told to work.
时不时地，有人会抓住你，然后让你去工作。

00:38:45.860 --> 00:38:55.179
One thing to remember, I think, is that if you go into TV and film, you are almost assuredly a fan of TV and film.
我认为要记住的一件事是，如果您进入电视和电影领域，您几乎肯定是电视和电影的粉丝。

00:38:55.179 --> 00:38:56.900
That's it, maybe you don't wanna live in that part of you, right?
就是这样，也许你不想生活在你的那一部分，对吗？

00:38:56.900 --> 00:39:02.380
Oh, Spike was probably psyched that it's like, oh my God, that's the showrunner of how much your mother, like I wanna know what I'm doing right now.
哦，斯派克可能很兴奋，天哪，这就是你妈妈的节目主持人，就像我想知道我现在在做什么。

00:39:02.380 --> 00:39:05.820
But he was there's, yeah.
但他就在那里，是的。

00:39:05.820 --> 00:39:21.546
I try to remember that, like, when I'm shocked that people are so disoriented when they meet me, I try to remember that like, I, I shared that back before I got behind the curtain of it all, you know, and now it's like, it's just my workplace.
我试着记住这一点，就像，当我对人们见到我时如此迷失方向感到震惊时，我试着记住，我，我在幕后分享了这一点，你知道，现在就像，这只是我的工作场所。

00:39:21.546 --> 00:39:25.947
You know, there's still, there's a, I'm not particularly starstruck.
你知道，还有，还有，我并不是特别追星。

00:39:25.947 --> 00:39:37.467
There are a few people that like can kind of make me a little wobbly, but I most of the time, I just, I know what they do, I know, you know, and I might respect them quite a bit.
有一些人喜欢会让我有点摇摆不定，但大多数时候，我只是，我知道他们做什么，我知道，你知道，而且我可能会非常尊重他们。

00:39:37.467 --> 00:39:41.609
And I would want to, you know, talk with them, but not in a way.
我想，你知道，与他们交谈，但不是以某种方式。

00:39:41.609 --> 00:39:49.505
I've spent so many years trying to humanize myself when I meet people like that to be like, I'm having lunch with my wife.
多年来，当我遇到这样的人时，我一直试图让自己变得人性化，就像我正在和我的妻子共进午餐一样。

00:39:49.505 --> 00:39:58.954
You're like, I'll take a moment, you know, but it's such a strange thing for people to not be expecting to see someone they know from TV in a day.
你会说，我会花点时间，你知道，但是对于人们来说，没有想到有一天会看到他们在电视上认识的人，这是一件很奇怪的事情。

00:39:58.954 --> 00:40:11.379
You know, Clooney said this, I remember, George Clooney He said this in a New Yorker profile that he said, I try to remember when people see me on the street, it's the high point of their day.
你知道，克鲁尼说过这样的话，我记得，乔治·克鲁尼在《纽约客》的一篇个人资料中说过这样的话，他说，我试着记住当人们在街上看到我时，那是他们一天的最高点。

00:40:11.380 --> 00:40:13.579
It's like the story they're gonna tell at the end of the day.
这就像他们在一天结束时要讲述的故事。

00:40:13.579 --> 00:40:16.059
And sometimes they really lose their minds.
有时他们真的会失去理智。

00:40:16.059 --> 00:40:25.539
And it's up to me at some point to ground them to get their name, to get them back in their body so they don't feel humiliated by the experience of meeting me.
我有责任在某个时候让他们禁足，让他们知道自己的名字，让他们回到自己的身体里，这样他们就不会因为见到我的经历而感到羞辱。

00:40:25.539 --> 00:40:26.900
So they can have like an experience of meeting me.
这样他们就可以有一种与我见面的经历。

00:40:26.900 --> 00:40:28.780
That's a really thoughtful take on that.
这真是一个深思熟虑的想法。

00:40:28.780 --> 00:40:29.619
That's very cool.
这非常酷。

00:40:29.619 --> 00:40:33.780
I've thought about it for a long time and I try to do that, like at my best I do that.
我已经考虑了很长时间，并且尝试这样做，就像我尽我所能那样做。

00:40:33.780 --> 00:40:40.019
Sometimes you have indolicate moments and some people probably think like that guy's not in his mind, but you know, you know, I do my best.
有时候你会有一些慵懒的时刻，有些人可能会认为那个人不在他的脑海里，但你知道，你知道，我尽力了。

00:40:40.619 --> 00:41:04.407
I literally had a moment like that on the other side of that because in my neighborhood Bob Balaban lives in my neighborhood and he's like the level of guy that like, you know, you see Bob Balaban is like, I like that's like, that's like, like serious star struck and I was with my daughter and we had just like, we were like literally watched the first 20 minutes of waiting for government like and then like went out to like get dinner and like saw him.
我确实也有过这样的时刻，因为在我的社区，鲍勃·巴拉班就住在我的社区，他就像这样的人，你知道，你看鲍勃·巴拉班就像是，我喜欢，就像，就像严肃的明星一样，我和我的女儿在一起，我们就好像，我们就像真的看着等待政府的前20分钟一样，然后就像出去吃晚饭一样，就像看到了他。

00:41:04.407 --> 00:41:11.778
And I had a moment where I like, I, you know, just just the fan and me just sort of took over and I was like, excuse me, are you Bob Balaban?
有那么一刻，我喜欢，你知道，只是粉丝和我就接管了，我想，对不起，你是鲍勃·巴拉班吗？

00:41:11.778 --> 00:41:14.497
He was like, yes, I was like, can I shake your hand?
他说，是的，我想，我可以握你的手吗？

00:41:14.497 --> 00:41:16.588
And he was like, oh, no, I'd rather not.
他说，哦，不，我不想。

00:41:16.588 --> 00:41:17.790
I just washed my hands.
我刚洗完手。

00:41:17.790 --> 00:41:31.278
And like, and in that moment, like, I just said it sort of, I tried to say casually, but like, he could have like, he could have kept walking and turned that into the story that I'm like running in my head, like I wouldn't have slept for a week if he hadn't.
就在那一刻，就像，我只是这么说，我试图随意地说，但是，就像，他可以像，他可以继续走，然后把它变成我在脑海中运行的故事，就像如果他不这样做，我一周都不会睡觉。

00:41:31.278 --> 00:41:37.500
But he was so sweet after that and and like talked to me and talked to my daughter and was like just absolutely lovely.
但在那之后他非常可爱，喜欢和我说话，和我女儿说话，非常可爱。

00:41:37.500 --> 00:41:44.820
And I mean, I'm still, I still have not slept since that moment and thinking about like, I shouldn't have tried to shake his hands.
我的意思是，从那一刻起我仍然没有睡过，我在想，我不应该试图与他握手。

00:41:44.820 --> 00:41:56.699
But like to any people out there, there is, I'm not like a super germophobic, but sometimes like after these shows, I've been doing on tour, like people really wanna shake your hand.
但就像对那里的任何人一样，我并不像一个超级细菌恐惧症患者，但有时就像在这些演出之后，我一直在巡回演出，就像人们真的想和你握手一样。

00:41:56.699 --> 00:42:03.260
And by the time you've shaken like 20 hands, It's like, you feel like you really got to sterilize.
当你握了大约 20 只手时，你会觉得你真的必须消毒了。

00:42:03.260 --> 00:42:04.619
Yeah, no, I, yeah.
是的，不，我，是的。

00:42:04.619 --> 00:42:07.940
Like in the moment, I heard myself saying, I was like, no, no, no, he doesn't want to eat something.
就像在那一刻，我听到自己说，我当时想，不，不，不，他不想吃东西。

00:42:07.940 --> 00:42:14.019
Like, cause it is, and also like, it sort of made me like culturally, we might, are we past hand shaking?
就像，因为它是，而且也像，它让我在文化上喜欢，我们可能，我们过去握手了吗？

00:42:14.019 --> 00:42:16.980
Maybe I was like, I don't, I don't really shake people's hands when I meet them.
也许我当时想，我不，当我见到别人时，我并没有真正与他们握手。

00:42:16.980 --> 00:42:21.579
Like I feel like maybe that's a, there were a lot of people during COVID that were like, I hope hand shaking is over.
我觉得，在新冠疫情期间，有很多人都说，我希望握手能够结束。

00:42:21.579 --> 00:42:22.420
Yeah.
是的。

00:42:22.420 --> 00:42:23.260
I think, yeah.
我想，是的。

00:42:23.260 --> 00:42:24.300
This bump is better for sure.
这个凹凸肯定更好。

00:42:24.300 --> 00:42:26.659
Yeah, courtly bows, I think it was supposed to come back.
是的，礼貌地鞠躬，我想它应该回来。

00:42:26.659 --> 00:42:31.659
Like that was gonna be the, My, uh, my wife, Jordana, uh, this is a section Carter.
就像那将是，我的，呃，我的妻子，乔丹娜，呃，这是卡特的一部分。

00:42:31.659 --> 00:42:41.789
I think you remember this, but we call it, uh, questions and observations from a clinical psychologist who's never seen how I met your mother and also happens to be married to Josh.
我想你记得这一点，但我们称之为，呃，来自一位临床心理学家的问题和观察，他从未见过我是如何认识你母亲的，而且碰巧与乔什结婚了。

00:42:42.670 --> 00:42:43.190
Uh, good title.
呃，好标题。

